  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sujit Kumar Sao vs The State Of Jharkhand ... .... Opposite ... on 7 July, 2021 Author: Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi Bench: Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi Cr.M.P. No. 700 of 2021 ------ 1.Sujit Kumar Sao 2.Ranjeet Kumar ... .... .... Petitioners Versus The State of Jharkhand ... .... Opposite Party Coram : Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi For the Petitioners : Mr. Nilesh Kumar, Advocate For the State : Mr. Prabhu Dayal Agrawal, A.P.P. 03/07.07.2021",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Mr. Nilesh Kumar, learned counsel for the petitioners undertakes to remove the defects within two weeks. Mr. Nilesh Kumar, learned counsel for the petitioners submits that Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 is special Act and unnecessarily sections of Indian Penal Code have been lodged. According to him it is well-settled law that if Special Act is there, cognizance cannot be taken under sections of Indian Penal Code. He submits that procedure laid down under section 42 of the Act has not been followed. Mr. Prabhu Dayal Agrawal, learned counsel for the State shall take instruction and file counter-affidavit within four weeks.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Mr. Nilesh Kumar, learned counsel for the petitioners undertakes to remove the defects within two weeks. Mr. Nilesh Kumar, learned counsel for the petitioners submits that Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 is special Act and unnecessarily sections of Indian Penal Code have been lodged. According to him it is well-settled law that if Special Act is there, cognizance cannot be taken under sections of Indian Penal Code. He submits that procedure laid down under section 42 of the Act has not been followed.",
    "respondent_arguments": "Mr. Prabhu Dayal Agrawal, learned counsel for the State shall take instruction and file counter-affidavit within four weeks.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
